  "editorial_note": "GitHub listed fifteen projects this Tuesday morning, and nine of them were featured here in the past week, so they stay out. Today's five picks are all first appearances: Arcane, a ==self-hosted Docker manager that just shipped version 3==; ffmpeg-skill, which gives coding agents a local video editor; Jiangshan Map, an interactive historical atlas of China; Google Research's PaperOrchestra for drafting research papers with agents; and last30days, the social-search skill behind part of this paper's own research. Curation order reflects practical interest, not GitHub rank. Trending is not a release date or an endorsement.",
  "coverage_notes": [
    "GitHub's daily listing held 15 rows at capture. The capture parsed exactly fifteen listing rows and is GitHub's own list, not a truncation by us.",
    "All 15 listing entries were inspected. Exact public GitHub API metadata of the six not-yet-featured entries was read between 07:01:00 and 07:01:04 UTC, their README files between 07:01:11 and 07:01:15 UTC, and recent releases before 07:01:51 UTC. Every checked repository was active and unarchived.",
    "Nine entries featured in the past seven days were left out: ag-ui-protocol/ag-ui and dream-num/univer (15 November), backnotprop/plannotator, tradermonty/claude-trading-skills, alibaba/open-code-review and ChromeDevTools/chrome-devtools-mcp (14 November), and elementalsouls/Claude-BugHunter, google-labs-code/stitch-skills and NVIDIA/SkillEvaluator (16 November). Their releases since those picks are patch builds or dated routine releases, or none at all, which we did not judge a material change.",
    "sveltejs/svelte was inspected and not picked: it is a mature, widely known framework whose latest release, svelte@5.57.3, dates from 26 October, so the listing gave no new reason to feature it today.",
    "Disclosure: The AI Gazette's twice-daily research step uses an earlier version of the last30days engine (mvanhorn/last30days-skill). It was picked on its own merits, and its card states its limits.",
    "Jiangshan Map is GPL-3.0 for its code and own data, but its prefecture-level boundary layer derives from CHGIS and stays under CHGIS terms (academic, non-commercial use, no redistribution), as its README states. The license field on its card shows GitHub's detection only.",
    "The preceding seven calendar dates, 10-16 November, were checked for local history; all seven editions exist.",
    "The official listing was captured at 08:00:49 Europe/Paris. Literal stars-today labels are GitHub's displayed period figures; API total stars and README evidence were checked separately at the times shown per card. They are not an independently audited rolling 24-hour growth measurement.",
    "Feature descriptions, adoption and performance figures come from each project's own README and release notes and are the maintainers' claims. No candidate code, installer, CLI, plugin, skill or model was installed, downloaded or run, and none of this is a security audit or endorsement."
  ],
