      "trending_rank": 6,
      "description": "A self-hosted web interface for managing Docker: containers, images, volumes, Compose projects and remote hosts from one dashboard, written in Go.",
      "why_interesting": "Version 3.0.0, published on 14 November, ==redesigns the dashboard and expands GitOps and backups==. The release notes also list live upgrade progress, update blocking based on image vulnerability scans, and renamed Arcane agents with mTLS enrollment for managing other hosts.",
      "caveat": "Version 3 is ==a breaking upgrade==: configuration variables gain an ARCANE_ prefix, legacy protocols, image tags and CLI flags are removed, and the polling agent is gone; the 2.x line lives on a separate branch. Like any Docker manager it needs the Docker daemon, which amounts to ==root access on the host==.",
